Z||000003||KRMFiero||05-25-2001||04:48 PM||||I know why you probley want to do it,  so you can have a tranny... i have did this before you have to put engine in the back and do alot of welding and cutting... if you seriously want to do this i will take pictured of the frame (I recently took it apart but you can still tell how it goes)<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||05-25-2001||05:05 PM||||top speed on a 12HP riding lawn mower is about 6mph. To go faster you would have to change pullys or gears somewhere to get the ratio up.<P>  the tranny on a riding lawnmower is not a plus, cause you cant shift it while you are moving on most setups.<P>  You get a riding lawn mower going more than 8 or 10mph and its gonna be squirrly - easy to tip over - unless its one of those ForrestGump snapper ones with the motor in the back.<P>  If you really want a go kart, decide what you want, figure out how much it will cost, imaging yourself having one already, then decide, how do you get There from Here.<P>   You would be surprized, you will find in most things in life, once you put your mind to it, it will happen easier than you think.<P>  If you want a GoKart, make it a goal for yourself, and get a real GoKart!||||reg||1
